# Git Workflow Rules

## Safety

- Inspect `git status` before making broad changes
- Keep changes focused on the user request
- Do not mix unrelated refactors into a feature or bug-fix change
- Never use destructive commands such as hard reset or checkout-revert unless explicitly requested

## Commit Quality

- Commit only after relevant linting, tests, or build validation for the touched area
- Keep commits small enough to review and roll back safely
- Do not commit secrets, `.env`, debug logs, or accidental build output
- Generated artifacts should be committed only when the workflow explicitly requires them

## Branching and Review Readiness

- Prefer short-lived branches for non-trivial work
- Summaries should describe the behavior change, not just the files touched
- If validation was skipped, call it out clearly in the final handoff
